{% comment %}
  Mobile above-the-fold corrections for the product gallery.

  Measured on the Purple Bearbrick page at 375x812 before this change:
    .tdp-thumbs wrapped 12 thumbnails onto 3 rows = 178px tall
    gallery total 528px, title y=741, price y=874, add-to-cart y=1205
  Price and CTA both sat below the fold, so paid traffic landed on an image
  with no price in view.

  Collapsing the thumbnail strip to one horizontally scrollable row and
  capping the hero image reclaims roughly 165px and lifts the price above
  the fold.

  These overrides belong in sections/diorama-product.liquid alongside the
  rest of the gallery CSS; they live here only to avoid rewriting that
  74KB file wholesale. Fold them in next time that file is edited.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if template.name == 'product' and product != blank -%}
  <style>
    @media (max-width: 749px) {
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumbs {
        flex-wrap: nowrap;
        overflow-x: auto;
        overflow-y: hidden;
        scrollbar-width: none;
        -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
      }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumbs::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-thumb { flex: 0 0 auto; }

      .tdp-gallery .tdp-main-img { max-height: 300px; }
      .tdp-gallery .tdp-main-img img {
        max-height: 300px;
        object-fit: contain;
      }
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP mobile fold fix",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
